Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Override inherited virtual abstract det_temp and pass-2 slots on backend ncg* classes
License: expat

Same root cause as the front-end `det_temp` patch, on the backend
side. The `ncg*` codegen units derive from base node classes that
declare `det_temp` and a couple of `pass_2`-related delegates as
`virtual; abstract;`. Native FPC reaches these methods only on
codegen-specialised metaclass subclasses; the bare backend classes
themselves are never asked to dispatch them.

tp2cc lowers each abstract Pascal method as a pure-virtual C++ method,
which makes the class non-instantiable in C++. Since the bootstrap
flow does construct these `ncg*` classes directly, the abstract slots
have to be filled. Add no-op `det_temp` overrides and the few trivial
`pass_2` delegates needed to keep each metaclass concrete. Behaviour
is unchanged in either compiler -- the methods just exist instead of
being abstract placeholders.

